challenge: >-
  Young people running market stalls, boda bodas, salons and chapati stands needed a coach on Telegram. It had to record daily sales and profit, answer business questions in their own language mix, never push a loan, and put their wellbeing ahead of business the moment someone was struggling. Telegram retries webhooks, so it also had to never reply twice.
solution: >-
  The SalnetHub team built the bot in n8n with Supabase Postgres: a router that classifies every message with an LLM and validates the JSON, four brain sub-workflows (Numbers, Coach, Care, Help), one Send Reply workflow that caps replies at 60 words and handles rate limits, and an error branch that alerts an admin instead of going silent. The bot is live and in use.
